WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.301
-Great to see you, Kenan,
how are you?

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:04.104
-Oh, great to see you, buddy.

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:05.905
Look at that, look at that hair!

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:08.308
I'm going right after it,
immediately.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:09.342
[ Laughter ]

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:10.443
-This is the last day...
-Love it.

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:13.278
-...before the haircut,
but you enjoy it.

00:00:13.278 --> 00:00:15.081
-I'm glad I caught it.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.549
-You know, I need this sort
of positive feedback

00:00:17.549 --> 00:00:19.252
to keep
my flowing locks flowing.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:20.520
So, thank you.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.955
-Yeah, I mean, even after,
you know, when you --

00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:26.325
after quarantine hopefully will
be over and stuff like that,

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:28.661
are you going to ever, like,
get back to growing it out?

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.062
Are you feeling
like a different dude?

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:31.964
-I don't know,
because we're never more than,

00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:33.967
like, two weeks off,

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:36.569
when we're actually
in the regular studio.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:39.472
So, this might be the last
hoorah, but it's been a good --

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:41.707
it's been a good, fun hoorah.

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:46.246
-I wanted it to be, like,
your next book cover, almost.

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:47.480
-You know, I haven't
written a book,

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.483
but I should take
some jacket covers now.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:51.651
-Well, your first book cover.

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:53.786
That should be some jacket
photo, for sure.

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:55.755
It's looking good.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:57.457
-How are your kids?

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:58.824
I know they're 6 and 2.

00:00:58.824 --> 00:01:01.460
How have they been hanging in?
-They've been good.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:03.763
They're, you know, they're --
my big girl's, like,

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.698
old enough to kind of know
what's going on,

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:09.635
but not old enough to be
missing anything, necessarily.

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:12.405
Like, she still runs into
a couple kids here and there,

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:15.941
you know, friends and family
and stuff like that, so.

00:01:15.941 --> 00:01:18.678
-Your 6-year-old, the people
she did get to see

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.514
were highlights for her,
because you were a guest judge

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:23.983
on "America's Got Talent."
-Yeah.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:26.485
-And Georgia's a fan, correct?

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:28.587
-She is a ginormous fan.

00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:31.023
I mean, she watches
it every day.

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:33.759
She knows all the contestants'
first and last names

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:35.428
and their stories,
you know what I mean?

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.830
It's like her first real dive

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.698
into something that's hers,
you know what I mean?

00:01:39.698 --> 00:01:41.967
And she watches
"Britain's Got Talent."

00:01:41.967 --> 00:01:43.436
She's going deep with it.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:44.870
-That's great.
How have you enjoyed it?

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.406
I know you're filling in
for Simon Cowell.

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:48.207
-Yeah, everybody was really warm
and welcoming,

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:50.276
and the acts were great.

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.344
It was a little hard
to watch people

00:01:52.344 --> 00:01:54.046
get sent home or whatever.

00:01:54.046 --> 00:01:55.047
-Sure, of course.

00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:56.515
-Georgia had a dream come true

00:01:56.515 --> 00:01:58.351
and that was good enough
for me, you know.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.419
She got to wave to everybody
and say what's up to

00:02:00.419 --> 00:02:02.354
Terry Crews, you know.

00:02:02.354 --> 00:02:06.792
And Terry Crews, oh, he's got
some real sharp radar

00:02:06.792 --> 00:02:08.794
on the color scheme
with those suits.

00:02:08.794 --> 00:02:10.230
-Yeah, oh, my God, absolutely.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:14.500
-That was a nice pumpkin spice,
silky, mm.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.136
For fall, getting everybody
ready for fall.

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:18.170
That was a good one.

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:20.506
-So, I have to ask,
the last time

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:21.941
you were on the show,
you were getting ready

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:25.478
for the Eddie Murphy-hosted
Christmas "SNL."

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:28.481
And I should apologize
to my viewers,

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.383
because every single person
who's been on the show

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:31.884
since then, I've asked about it.

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:35.455
But I am so jealous
that I didn't get to be there.

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:37.690
Just watching it at home
was such a joy.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.091
What was it like --
-Yeah, where were you?

00:02:39.091 --> 00:02:41.094
-What?
-Where were you?

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:43.496
-I was just --
I don't know where I was.

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:46.165
I guess I should have come,
but it was so much fun to watch.

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:48.367
-You guys were
on holiday already.

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:50.069
-We were probably were
on holiday already, yeah.

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:54.140
-On holiday, as I --
-On holiday.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:57.376
-Yes, on holiday.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.376 --> 00:03:00.712
-How was the week?

00:03:00.712 --> 00:03:02.415
-So surreal, honestly.

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:05.985
Like, you're looking at a guy,
especially for me,

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.454
who's just been bigger than life

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:11.157
for my entire existence,
you know what I mean?

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:12.525
And now he's sitting
in front of me,

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:15.962
he's looking me in my eye,
calling me by my name.

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.664
We're conversating,
we go to, like,

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:19.164
the host dinner and all of that.

00:03:19.164 --> 00:03:21.434
It's just very intimate
all of a sudden, with,

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:24.336
like, one of your greatest,
greatest heroes, you know?

00:03:24.336 --> 00:03:25.939
And it was incredible.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:27.406
Six days of that, you know?

00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:30.376
And he just got more and more
comfortable with everybody

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.178
and more open
and cracking jokes.

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:33.813
And by the time
we were doing, like,

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.715
Thursday promos
with Lizzo,

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:38.050
he was just, like, all into it,
you know what I mean?

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:40.786
Having a great time and laughing
and, like,

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:42.421
Lizzo made him
laugh in the promo,

00:03:42.421 --> 00:03:44.190
and that's the one
that they used.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.525
And it just looked like
everybody's energy

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:48.627
was towards him
in a positive way,

00:03:48.627 --> 00:03:50.462
wanting him to have
a great show.

00:03:50.462 --> 00:03:51.764
It was amazing.

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.766
-The thing that I realized,
as well,

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:58.737
from watching that episode
is you realize he is joy.

00:03:58.737 --> 00:04:01.006
He's just joy incarnate
as a sketch performer.

00:04:01.006 --> 00:04:03.909
And even, you know,
in the sketch

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:08.514
where he made a bad cake,
he still presented it as joyful.

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:10.216
Like, he was smiling
through everything.

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:12.085
And I realize, like, you guys --

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:14.053
you and he have the same DNA
as performers.

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:17.323
Like, you're very positive,
joyous.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:19.559
It's contagious,
the way you perform.

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.227
And I can't believe I'm saying
this, Kenan,

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:24.863
but you are now coming
into your 18th season on "SNL."

00:04:24.863 --> 00:04:27.132
-Isn't that crazy?
-It's crazy.

00:04:27.132 --> 00:04:29.534
-Isn't that crazy?
-Well, one reason it's crazy

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:30.803
is you look the same,

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:33.539
so that's one part
that makes it crazy.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:34.874
-Thank you.
I've got my beard going.

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:38.444
There's a beard here.
You can see it.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:40.079
Well, you know, if anything,

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:42.782
I definitely took that from him,
you know what I'm saying?

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:45.651
Just because he was
the first person

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:49.789
to show me what it was like
to just present joy

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:51.290
in every performance, basically.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.792
Like, all he ever
was going after

00:04:53.792 --> 00:04:55.694
was a joyous reaction
from people.

00:04:55.694 --> 00:04:58.631
He's really entertaining,
like, for real, for real.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.733
And yeah, I always, you know,

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.902
just migrated towards
that kind of thing

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:05.838
because it makes me
feel good in the process.

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:08.173
-Yeah.
Does it get --

00:05:08.173 --> 00:05:12.011
I mean, at what point in that
18 years did you start feeling,

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:13.379
as the fall
was rolling around --

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:16.015
and again, this is a unique fall
we're rolling into --

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:19.852
but, you know, I remember having
anxiety and anxiety and anxiety,

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:21.954
until about season six or seven,
when I thought,

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:24.723
"Okay, I think I at least know

00:05:24.723 --> 00:05:27.794
enough of the ropes here
to feel somewhat comfortable."

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:29.862
When did that start for you?

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:33.265
-I mean, I feel like it got

00:05:33.265 --> 00:05:35.835
comfortable,
like, right around

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:38.871
when I started to land a sketch
that was my own idea.

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:40.672
Like, kind of after
"Scared Straight,"

00:05:40.672 --> 00:05:42.508
and I really started being able

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:44.610
to build connections
with writers for real,

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.012
as opposed to just, like,
a writer giving me something

00:05:47.012 --> 00:05:50.082
and being able to, like, really
build something from scratch.

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:51.483
And then I was like, "Oh, now

00:05:51.483 --> 00:05:54.153
I have a different kind
of relationship with the show,"

00:05:54.153 --> 00:05:55.454
you know what I mean,
as opposed to, like,

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:57.456
cast/writer separation
or anything like that.

00:05:57.456 --> 00:06:00.026
I felt more intertwined

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:02.295
with the entire process
finally, you know?

00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:05.531
And then I also just never
felt like

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:07.633
I was alone
in building the show.

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:08.567
There's so many people.

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:10.236
Like, just watching the stress

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:11.470
that you would go through,
you know?

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.538
And like, you were one
of the most perfect --

00:06:13.538 --> 00:06:16.175
it looked like it would
come easy to you type of writers

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:18.677
I had ever seen,
between like you and Tina.

00:06:18.677 --> 00:06:20.078
It looked like you could just

00:06:20.078 --> 00:06:21.613
flush out sketches,
you, Tina, and Joe.

00:06:21.613 --> 00:06:25.251
Almost like you almost crap
them out, like it's nothing.

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:29.355
But, to also watch how on-edge
and on your toes

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:30.856
you were all week,

00:06:30.856 --> 00:06:32.492
you know what I mean,
just, like, taught me,

00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:34.660
"Oh, this is a continuous
type of process."

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.062
So, yeah, I still feel
it coming around.

00:06:37.062 --> 00:06:39.498
Like, I feel, you know,
September creeping up

00:06:39.498 --> 00:06:40.866
and October creeping up,

00:06:40.866 --> 00:06:43.168
and it's like, yeah,
you should be prepared.

00:06:43.168 --> 00:06:45.003
I need to go in there with,
like, a couple pitches,

00:06:45.003 --> 00:06:47.906
because every time I come in
after the summer lately

00:06:47.906 --> 00:06:49.942
and I pitch to Tucker,
I've been thinking

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:51.777
like a whole summer's
worth of ideas.

00:06:51.777 --> 00:06:55.548
And I pitch him like six
and he likes, like, half of one.

00:06:55.548 --> 00:06:58.250
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:01.120
-What about -- I know you've got
a podcast now as well.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:04.189
It must be nice, because again,
we know you so much as,

00:07:04.189 --> 00:07:06.892
you know,
somebody who's a great character

00:07:06.892 --> 00:07:09.028
performer or impressions.

00:07:09.028 --> 00:07:11.864
Is it fun to just
get to be Kenan?

00:07:11.864 --> 00:07:13.465
-Oh, it's great.

00:07:13.465 --> 00:07:15.835
It's so much --
I can just relax and be myself

00:07:15.835 --> 00:07:18.103
and not have any kind
of expectation

00:07:18.103 --> 00:07:19.605
on what's supposed to happen.

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:23.075
Like, comedy, we're supposed to
be going for some kind of laugh,

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:26.145
if we're going to be wasting
people's time with noise

00:07:26.145 --> 00:07:28.147
and words, right,
you know what I mean?

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:29.815
Like, we're supposed to be,
like,

00:07:29.815 --> 00:07:31.384
setting up and punchlining.

00:07:31.384 --> 00:07:32.484
But, with the podcast,
it's like,

00:07:32.484 --> 00:07:33.719
we're just having
a conversation

00:07:33.719 --> 00:07:36.355
and this is the first time
I think people can,

00:07:36.355 --> 00:07:38.157
you know, get a real
sense of me

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:41.327
outside of an eight-minute
talk show segment or something.

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:42.795
-Well, that's great, buddy.

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:46.565
I really hope you guys figure
out some version of the show.

00:07:46.565 --> 00:07:49.368
We all will be looking forward
to "SNL's" season

00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:51.137
premiere in any form...
-Oh, it's going to happen.

00:07:51.137 --> 00:07:53.572
-...it comes in.
-It's gonna happen.

00:07:53.572 --> 00:07:55.274
-I'm very excited to hear that.

00:07:55.274 --> 00:07:56.775
It's always great to see you,
buddy.

00:07:56.775 --> 00:07:58.577
-You, too, buddy.
You enjoy.

00:07:58.577 --> 00:08:01.314
Please, send me a lock
of that hair, please.

00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:02.515
-I will. I will.

